            "application/vnd.google.colaboratory.intrinsic+json": {
              "type": "dataframe",
              "variable_name": "df_readable",
              "summary": "{\n  \"name\": \"df_readable\",\n  \"rows\": 97219,\n  \"fields\": [\n    {\n      \"column\": \"prompt\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"string\",\n        \"num_unique_values\": 97219,\n        \"samples\": [\n          \"After you are sent to prison , all the inmates slowly disappear , one by one..\",\n          \"Technology invents a way for humans to produce dreams for others to see , and pretty soon *Dream Movies* are being rented out overnight . Only this time , the movie freezes while you 're in the middle of it .\",\n          \"it 's discovered that due to a virus , humanity is no longer able to produce children , the people that are alive today are the last . Follow the story from one of humanities last family 's\"\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"human_story\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"string\",\n        \"num_unique_values\": 97214,\n        \"samples\": [\n          \"The first alien to land on Earth had shocked the globe . Aliens were no longer a thing of legend or wonder , as here stood an entire ship full of the otherworldly creatures . <newline> <newline> They were called the Kaltzbarchs . <newline> <newline> They were all humanoid , except that they had a far wider range of skin , hair , and eye pigments . But human wer e still , which was found outafter taking several tests to insure they hand brought us a deadly virus from their home planet . <newline> <newline> One of Kaltzbachs ' first conditions of peace was very simple , yet ultimately shocking . Though , in retrospective , it made sense . <newline> <newline> `` This 'Miss Universe ' pageant you Earthlings have ... `` said their leader during the widely viewed press conference between him and President Obama . `` Your planet has no other species running except for your own . What we ask for is that we be able to enter our own candidate , and that she be given a fair shot. `` <newline> <newline> And so it was done . They had chosen the most Earthly looking woman they had , a gorgeous bombshell named Kalique who had the most hauntingly beautiful purple eyes any one had ever seen , and beautiful black hair that shone blue in light . <newline> <newline> Half of the judges were aliens , though everyone agreed that it was a mistake to rehire Steve Harvey . <newline> <newline> This became clear when the crowning moment came about . The final three stood on stage , ignoring the cold gazes of the rest of the girls they had beaten . <newline> <newline> Miss Korea , Miss Spain , and Miss Kaltzbach all stood , barely hidden smirks in their faces as Steve took the card from the very important envelope . <newline> <newline> The previous Miss Universe , the stunning former Miss Philippines Pia Wartzbach , looked nervously between the paper , the girls , and Steve . Like the rest of the world , she had not yet forgotten his blunder the year before . <newline> <newline> `` The second runner up is ... Miss Spain ! `` <newline> <newline> Miss Spain , the beautiful brunette bombshell , accepted her tiara and flowers with thinly veiled disappointment . Now there were the final two . <newline> <newline> Both worlds held their breaths . Another mistake could potentially cause an intergalactic war ... <newline> <newline> `` And Miss Universe 2016 is ... ! `` Steve took care to analyze the card properly this time . `` Wait a minute ... Pia ? `` <newline> <newline> Pia walked towards him and gazed at the card , and then blinked in shock . <newline> <newline> Steve wiped away the sweat gathering on his brow , and looked up at the cameras . <newline> <newline> `` Miss Universe 2016 is ... both Miss Korea and Miss Kaltzbach ! `` <newline> <newline> Silence . <newline> <newline> Kalique 's eye twitched as they suddenly brought out another crown , this time carried in by the former Miss Columbia . <newline> <newline> Cheers erupted , suddenly understanding the situation . It had been a plan all along for peace between the two planets . <newline> <newline> Or at least that was what the leaders thought . What the audience had all been thinking was that shit could have definitely gone down , and everyone was thankful it had n't . <newline> <newline> The end <newline> <newline>\",\n          \"Name : Carl Richmond <newline> <newline> Age : 43 <newline> <newline> Approximate time of death : 8:45 P.M. , December 15 , 2014 <newline> <newline> Cause of death : Murder <newline> <newline> At approximately 8:40 P.M. , Mrs. Regina Richmond complained to her husband that the heat was no longer working in their house . Mr. Richmond and his son Robert went downstairs to investigate , and upon inspection discovered that the furnace had been turned off . After retrieving a flashlight , Mr. Richmond brushed some dust off of the furnace and reset it . As he did so , he noticed a large open box that was rapidly vibrating on the ground beneath the furnace . He opened the box to find it full of killer African bees , all of which immediately attacked Mr. Richmond . At this time , he had an apparent allergic reaction to the dust , and began to sneeze violently . During one of these sneezes , he inadvertently inhaled a bee which stung his tonsils , causing immediate swelling and asphyxiation . At the current time we believe his son Robert to be the main suspect- interviews with Robert revealed that he believed Christmas was on the 15th and not the 25th , which made him very angry with his father for not getting him any gifts .\",\n          \"I decided there was only one way this was going to happen . I was going to have to sell myself to other men . I tried a few upscale bars and night clubs . In the most bitter sweet way business was good . In twenty four hours I had an extremely sore jaw amongst other things . By the end of the 24 hours I had made the money for my wife 's operation . <newline> <newline> I walk in and she asks `` how much did you raise '' weakly . I told her the exact number . one hundred thousand dollars and five cents . `` Who gave you five cents ? '' she asked curiously but enthusiastic . `` Every damn one of them but it 'll be worth it when you have the rack of our dreams . ''\"\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"gpt_story\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"string\",\n        \"num_unique_values\": 97218,\n        \"samples\": [\n          \"In the dimly lit cell of Redwood Penitentiary, a place notorious for holding the most dangerous criminals, James Parker sat alone, contemplating the choices that had led him to this desolate confinement. Sentenced to life imprisonment for a crime he did not commit, hope seemed to flee his mind with each passing day. <newline>  <newline> But as time wore on, a peculiar occurrence began to unravel within the prison walls. One by one, the inmates seemed to vanish into thin air, leaving behind nothing but empty bunks and unanswered questions. <newline>  <newline> First, it was Tommy \\\"The Knife\\\" Malone, known for his merciless acts of violence. One night, James awoke to find Tommy's bed vacant, the sheets cold and untouched. The guards were baffled, searching every corner of the prison, but he was nowhere to be found. Rumors quickly spread among the remaining prisoners, whispers of supernatural forces at play. <newline>  <newline> As the days turned into weeks, more and more inmates disappeared, leaving James and a small handful of others to witness the growing mystery. Even the most hardened criminals grew fearful, their tough facades crumbling as their numbers diminished. Some whispered of an otherworldly curse, while others believed it to be the work of a sophisticated escape plan. <newline>  <newline> James, curious and desperate for answers, delved deeper into the strange phenomenon. He spent his days studying the prison's history, scouring the library for any clues that might shed light on the disappearances. No stone was left unturned. <newline>  <newline> One evening, as he sat alone in his cell, he stumbled upon an old newspaper article hidden among the dusty books. The article told a chilling tale of an ambitious warden who, years ago, had orchestrated a secret experiment. He had used the inmates as subjects, testing an unproven technology designed to transport them out of the prison and into different dimensions. <newline>  <newline> With growing excitement, James realized that he had stumbled upon the truth. The missing inmates were not vanishing into nothingness but were being transported to unknown realms. The experiment hadn't been intended for this purpose, yet the warden's reckless actions had set these events into motion. <newline>  <newline> Determined to uncover the prison's secrets, James rallied the remaining prisoners. They worked together, discovering hidden passages and forgotten rooms scattered throughout the prison. Along the way, they encountered strange and inexplicable phenomena\\u2014a world that existed beyond human comprehension. <newline>  <newline> As they ventured deeper into the prison's underbelly, they finally found the warden's secret laboratory. Amidst the abandoned machinery and flickering lights, they discovered the key to breaking the spell that had trapped them within these walls. <newline>  <newline> With courage and determination, James and his fellow inmates activated the machinery, reversing the effects of the experiment that had haunted them for so long. They were finally free, liberated from the clutches of their spectral prison. <newline>  <newline> Years later, whispers of the vanishing inmates would become the stuff of legend. But for James Parker, it was a reminder that even in the darkest of places, hope and perseverance could triumph over the most unimaginable circumstances.\",\n          \"Anna loved to indulge in the latest technological advancements, whether it was a new smartphone or a cutting-edge virtual reality headset. So, when she heard about the revolutionary invention that allowed people to produce dreams for others to see, she couldn't resist the temptation to experience it firsthand. <newline>  <newline> The concept was simple yet fascinating. With the help of a small device, anyone could record their dreams and convert them into a visual format. Soon, these dream movies became quite popular, and rental outlets began offering them for overnight use. <newline>  <newline> One evening, Anna visited her favorite store, DreamVision, in search of the perfect dream movie. She scanned the shelves filled with countless options, each boasting unique and immersive experiences. Finally, she settled on a movie titled \\\"Enchanting Skies.\\\" <newline>  <newline> Excited, Anna plugged the dream movie device into her brain interface and settled down in her bed. As the movie began, vibrant colors and surreal landscapes unfolded before her eyes. She found herself soaring through the cotton candy clouds, feeling the soft caress of the wind against her face. The dream movie seemed to be living up to its promise, taking her on an unforgettable journey through her own imagination. <newline>  <newline> However, just as she was about to reach the climax of the dream movie, the image froze. Anna blinked, thinking it was a technical glitch, but the screen remained motionless. Confusion replaced her excitement, and a flicker of panic took hold. <newline>  <newline> She attempted to remove the device, but it felt stuck in place. Sweat trickled down her forehead as her heart rate quickened. She was trapped, suspended in a dream-turned-nightmare. <newline>  <newline> Anna's mind raced, searching for a solution. She squeezed her eyes shut, hoping it would jolt her back to reality. But that didn't work either. Panic began to consume her, and she started thrashing around in her bed, desperate to wake up. <newline>  <newline> As seconds turned to minutes, and minutes turned to what felt like an eternity, Anna's despair deepened. She began to question whether she would ever escape this torment. The very technology that once fascinated her now threatened to imprison her forever. <newline>  <newline> Just when it seemed all hope was lost, a flicker of movement caught Anna's eye. The dream movie resumed, picking up from where it had frozen. Relief washed over her as she finally completed the dream experience she had signed up for. <newline>  <newline> But as Anna lay in bed, her heart still racing, she couldn't shake off the lingering sense of unease. The dream movie had changed her perception of technology, reminding her that sometimes, even the most alluring advancements could turn into nightmares. <newline>  <newline> From that day forward, Anna approached technology with caution. While she appreciated the wonders it could bring, she also understood the importance of being mindful of its potential consequences.\",\n          \"The world had changed. In the twilight of human existence, a somber truth had emerged \\u2013 a virus that had gradually rendered humanity unable to reproduce. The people alive today were the last, the final flickering flames in a world about to be extinguished. <newline>  <newline> In a small town nestled among rolling hills, the Thompson family bore the weight of this knowledge. Mark and Emily Thompson, along with their young daughter, Sarah, had become acutely aware that they carried the fate of humanity upon their shoulders. <newline>  <newline> Days were spent in a haze of uncertainty and fear, as the community struggled to come to terms with their impending extinction. Mark, the patriarch of the family, grappled with the burden of preserving the knowledge and achievements of generations past. He sought solace in the dusty attic of their family home, surrounded by history in the form of books, art, and photographs. Stories written by great thinkers, brushes of long-lost painters, and captured memories that had once seemed everlasting were now relics of a bygone era. <newline>  <newline> Emily, the matriarch, grappled with the steady stream of emotion that swept over her. She mourned the future that would never be, the laughter of grandchildren that would never ring through their home. But within her heart, a fierce determination grew. She would cherish each precious second with Sarah, instilling within her the knowledge and love of a world that would cease to exist. <newline>  <newline> Sarah, at only ten years old, had yet to truly comprehend the weight of their situation. She reveled in the simple joys of a child's imagination, finding solace in the vibrant colors of her drawings. With her innocent mind, she saw possibility amidst the darkness. Her laughter echoed through their home, a ray of hope in an otherwise desolate landscape. <newline>  <newline> The Thompsons lived each day as if it were their last, seizing every opportunity to savor the wonders of the natural world. They walked barefoot through fields of wildflowers, their feet sinking into the soft earth. They marveled at the changing seasons, knowing that they were witnessing the final dance of nature's cycles. <newline>  <newline> As the town united in the face of despair, they clung to the bonds of community. The final months were spent sharing stories, preserving traditions, and creating new memories. They organized gatherings to celebrate humanity's legacy, culminating in a grand farewell feast under the starlit sky. <newline>  <newline> In the moments before dawn broke on the last day, the Thompson family stood hand in hand on a hill overlooking the world they knew. In that quiet moment, they felt the weight of their responsibility, the legacy they would leave behind. They gazed at the sun cresting the horizon, knowing that it marked the end of an era. <newline>  <newline> As the darkness receded, painting the heavens in hues of gold, they took solace in the knowledge that the spirit of humanity would live on. It would resonate within the stories they had told, the art they had created, and the love they had shared. And as they watched the sun rise for the last time, they whispered a final goodbye to a world that was no longer theirs, carrying with them the hopes and dreams of a species that would forever be remembered.\"\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"
